			"text": "CAT4 — Students invent process strategies when teaching is thin\nRQ2 · finding",
			"x": 140,
			"y": -80,
			"width": 400,
			"height": 100,
			"color": "4"
		},
		{
			"id": "cases",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "Cases\nS1 S2 S3 S5 S7 S8 S9 S10",
			"x": -220,
			"y": -80,
			"width": 300,
			"height": 70,
			"color": "3"
		},
		{
			"id": "memo_group",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Memos** (8) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[S1M2]] — worked examples bridge text and diagram\n- [[S2M2]] — examples and professor check substitute for process\n- [[S3M2]] — professor feedback as correctness gate\n- [[S5M3]] — early sharing and self-initiated drafts replace waiting\n- [[S7M1]] — board labs split starters from copiers\n- [[S8M1]] — modelling arrived as a project requirement first\n- [[S9M1]] — start waits on seeing it done once\n- [[S10M2]] — reserved starter: notebook yes, board no",
			"x": -330,
			"y": 206,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 304,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "code_group",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Codes** (26) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[S1-C13]] — text-to-model via trial and error\n- [[S1-C15]] — no remembered step-by-step teaching\n- [[S1-C23]] — learn modelling best from worked examples\n- [[S2-C11]] — trial and error then ask professor\n- [[S2-C14]] — replicate reasoning from completed examples\n- [[S2-C15]] — start with objects then draw relationships\n- [[S2-C17]] — elements taught not explicit modelling process\n- [[S3-C07]] — waited for professor feedback to feel sure\n- [[S3-C13]] — picks first option when two seem valid\n- [[S3-C18]] — slides alone not enough without feedback\n- [[S5-C04]] — drafts version one without waiting for demo\n- [[S5-C07]] — small prototype settles modelling disagreements\n- [[S5-C14]] — wants weekly assessed diagram peer reviews\n- [[S7-C02]] — simple board example then class bullet-list\n- [[S7-C03]] — classmates copy the board instead of trying\n- [[S7-C04]] — starts fast to survive random board pick\n- [[S7-C05]] — teacher stays quiet until students debate\n- [[S8-C01]] — bachelor project required models without teaching them\n- [[S8-C03]] — underlines requirements then pencil-to-pen sketch\n- [[S8-C04]] — examples help notation more than expected answer\n- [[S9-C01]] — Covid online classes made shared modelling messy\n- [[S9-C02]] — teacher solves first then explains notation and why\n- [[S9-C03]] — needs to see it done once before starting alone\n- [[S10-C07]] — stays quiet at the board even with a ready solution\n- [[S10-C08]] — small public doubts go unresolved\n- [[S10-C14]] — desk walk-around beats raising a hand",
			"x": 540,
			"y": 206,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 808,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "explainer",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "What this means\n\nWhen the course does not spell out a process, students invent their own — trial and error, early drafts, pencil-to-pen sketches, notebook-then-board, or starting fast so they have something if picked at random.",
			"x": 80,
			"y": -360,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 180,
			"color": "1"
		}
	],
